-16 153x163, 08-18 113x157, 08-20 25x134, landing 2023-08-23 12:33 UTC. Ecliptic plane; orbit phase schematic.",[683,685,688,691,694,697],[53,120,684],36500,[64,686,687],173,41762,[227,689,690],226,41603,[262,692,693],228,51400,[309,695,696],233,71351,[381,698,699],236,127609,[701,704,706,709,712,715,718],[79,702,703],164,18074,[84,120,705],4313,[89,707,708],174,1437,[93,710,711],150,177,[97,713,714],153,163,[106,716,717],113,157,[110,719,720],25,134,"Chandrayaan-3","LANDER · ROVER · FLOWN","First soft-landing near the lunar south pole","Following the loss of Chandrayaan-2's Vikram lander in 2019, ISRO's third lunar mission was deliberately conservative — focused on the lander rather than carrying an orbiter. Vikram touched down at 69.4° S latitude, the closest any spacecraft had come to a lunar pole at the time (IM-2 landed closer in 2025). The Pragyan rover made the first in-situ measurement of sulfur near the lunar south pole and took in-situ thermal measurements. India became the fourth nation to soft-land on the Moon, landing closer to a lunar pole than any spacecraft before it — a region where future water-ice mining may become possible.",[726,730,733,736,739,744],{"met":53,"label":727,"note":728,"type":729},"LAUNCH","LVM3 M4 (formerly GSLV Mk III) from Sriharikota.","nominal",{"met":79,"label":731,"note":732,"type":729},"LOI","Lunar orbit insertion (multiple Earth and lunar orbit-raising burns used).",{"met":101,"label":734,"note":735,"type":729},"LANDER SEPARATION","Vikram lander separates from propulsion module.",{"met":15,"label":737,"note":738,"type":729},"TOUCHDOWN","Vikram lands at Shiv Shakti Point near south pole 2023-08-23 12:33 UTC.",{"met":740,"label":741,"note":742,"type":743},40.5,"PRAGYAN DEPLOYED","Rover rolls down ramp; begins surface science.","info",{"met":745,"label":746,"note":747,"type":743},53,"LUNAR NIGHT","Lander/rover put into hibernation as lunar night begins.","/orrery/images/missions/chandrayaan3/03.webp"],"uses":{"params":["id"]}}]}
